cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FPN Hub: Public Technical Overview"
message: "For scientific discussion of the public benchmark results, please cite the preferred citation below."
authors:
  - family-names: Skalski
    given-names: Sebastian
repository-code: "https://github.com/webkontakt2-arch/fpn-hub"
url: "https://fpn-systems.com/"
date-released: "2026-06-01"
license-url: "https://github.com/webkontakt2-arch/fpn-hub/blob/main/LICENSE"
abstract: >
  Public technical overview of FPN Hub, a PCT-pending deterministic topology
  framework for quantum processor architecture. The repository provides public
  technical framing and an IP-safe benchmark methodology summary. Selected
  benchmark results are publicly available in the associated Zenodo preprint,
  while protected topology construction logic, generators, coupling maps, and
  non-public implementation materials are not disclosed.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum processor architecture
  - topology
  - transpilation
  - benchmarking
  - routing
  - modular quantum computing
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: Skalski
      given-names: Sebastian
  title: "IP-Safe Routing Benchmarks for a Protected Modular Qubit Interconnect: Nonlocality Stress Tests, Compiler Cross-Checks, and Baseline-Specific Trade-offs"
  year: 2026
  doi: "10.5281/zenodo.21308015"
  url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21308015"
